Description: Kavis device to device sharing
 Sends files between devices on the same network with no account, no
 cloud and no server in the middle: the bytes go straight from one
 machine to the other (decision 11).
 .
 The protocol is LocalSend's, deliberately. A sharing feature that only
 talks to other Kavis machines is one nobody can use — the phone in the
 room runs Android and the laptop runs Windows, and LocalSend already
 exists on both. Speaking its protocol costs a UDP announcement and
 three HTTP endpoints and is the difference between "send this to my
 phone" working and not.
 .
 The hostname and the user name are never announced: a device that
 shouts who is sitting in front of it across a cafe network has told
 every stranger there. The default name is two random words.
